{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>For.</b> A little, in days, and my fury and my wrath against them will be finished, because of the multitude of their destruction. Some interpret their end like מאחרי בלותי (Genesis 18:12), on the analogy of תכליתם (Psalms 139:22):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The bracketed correction [צ\"ל תכלית] indicates that the received text reads תכליתם but should read תכלית; the final mem in Ibn Ezra's Hebrew citation is retained."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:17.418693115Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}